&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Two Six Technologies, we build, deploy, and implement innovative products that solve the world’s most complex challenges today. Through unrivaled collaboration and unwavering trust, we push the boundaries of what’s possible to empower our team and support our customers in building a safer global future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated, proactive, and adaptable&lt;strong&gt; Administrative Assistant &lt;/strong&gt;to provide comprehensive administrative and operational support to a fast-paced executive and their team in Laurel, MD.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone who thrives in a dynamic, high-demand environment and is comfortable balancing multiple competing priorities while maintaining a positive, can-do attitude. The ideal candidate is a self-starter who anticipates needs, takes initiative, and is willing to jump in wherever needed to keep the executive and team operating efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional desk-based administrative position. The successful candidate must be comfortable being constantly on the move, managing day-to-day administrative responsibilities, coordinating projects, handling physical tasks, and running errands throughout the day. No two days will look the same, and priorities may shift quickly. The ability to go with the flow, think on your feet, and get things done without needing constant direction is essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Administrative Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform a wide range of administrative tasks, including complex calendar management, scheduling, deconflicting competing priorities, preparing meeting materials and reports, and managing internal and external communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meeting &amp;amp; Travel Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate domestic and international travel arrangements, itineraries, and associated logistics. Plan and execute internal and external business meetings, conferences, and team events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project &amp;amp; Team Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as an internal coordinator and project manager to ensure various projects, initiatives, and action items are progressing on schedule. Follow up with stakeholders and proactively identify outstanding items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Day-to-Day Operational Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Handle a variety of administrative and operational tasks to support the executive and team, including document preparation, office coordination, supply management, and other duties as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Errands &amp;amp; Hands-On Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Frequently travel locally to complete errands, pick up and deliver items, coordinate services, and handle other in-person requests. Must be comfortable with a role that involves significant movement throughout the day and physical, hands-on responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactive Problem-Solving: &lt;/strong&gt;Anticipate the needs of the executive and team, identify potential issues before they arise, and independently find solutions without waiting for direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Responsiveness:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain consistent communication with the executive and team, remain accessible by phone, and respond promptly to changing priorities and time-sensitive requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt; Take on other administrative, operational, and special projects as needed. Be willing to step outside traditional administrative responsibilities to ensure the team has what it needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications &amp;amp; Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years of experience with Google Suite, Slack, Zoom, Microsoft Office Suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years of experience with meeting/event planning, and task management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational, time-management, and multitasking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage competing priorities and adjust quickly when schedules or needs change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-motivated with the ability to work independently and take initiative without constant oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive, can-do attitude with a willingness to jump in and tackle tasks of all sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to remain calm, professional, and solution-oriented in a high-pressure environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable performing hands-on tasks and being physically active throughout the workday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have reliable personal transportation and the ability to run local errands throughout the DMV area multiple times throughout the day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be available to work on-site in Laurel, MD, five days per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work outside traditional business hours, including before 9:00 AM and after 5:00 PM, as business needs require.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be accessible by phone and responsive to the executive and team&#39;s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a true &quot;no task is too big or too small&quot; mentality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is always thinking one step ahead and anticipating what needs to be done next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Doesn&#39;t wait to be told what to do and takes ownership of responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is comfortable with ambiguity and can pivot quickly when priorities change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoys staying busy and prefers a role where they are constantly moving rather than sitting behind a desk all day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is dependable, resourceful, and willing to go the extra mile to support the executive and team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can roll with the punches, maintain a positive attitude, and find a way to get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clearance/Citizenship:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain a Secret Clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI- MS1&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#onsite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two Six Technologies is committed to providing competitive and comprehensive compensation packages that reflect the value we place on our employees and their contributions. We believe in rewarding skills, experience, and performance. Our offerings include but are not limited to, medical, dental, and vision insurance, life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, paid leave, tuition assistance and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The projected salary range listed for this position is annualized. This is a general guideline and not a guarantee of salary. Salary is one component of our total compensation package and the specific salary offered is determined by various factors, including, but not limited to education, experience, knowledge, skills, geographic location, as well as contract specific affordability and organizational requirements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$40 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_PageFooter&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Looking for other great opportunities? Check out &lt;a href=&quot;https://twosixtech.com/careers/current-opportunities/&quot;&gt;Two Six Technologies Opportunities&lt;/a&gt; for all our Company’s current openings!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to make the first move towards growing your career? If so, check out the &lt;a href=&quot;https://twosixtech.com/careers/candidate-resources/&quot;&gt;Two Six Technologies Candidate Journey&lt;/a&gt;!&amp;nbsp; This will give you step-by-step directions on applying, what to expect during the application process, information about our rich benefits and perks along with our most frequently asked questions.&amp;nbsp; If you are undecided and would like to learn more about us and how we are contributing to essential missions, check out our&amp;nbsp; &lt;a href=&quot;https://twosixtech.com/about/news/&quot;&gt;Two Six Technologies News &lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;page!&amp;nbsp; We share information about the tech world around us and how we are making an impact!&amp;nbsp; Still have questions, no worries!&amp;nbsp; You can reach us at &lt;a href=&quot;https://twosixtech.com/contact/&quot;&gt;Contact Two Six Technologies&lt;/a&gt;. We are happy to connect and cover the information needed to assist you in reaching your next career milestone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two Six Technologies is an Equal Opportunity Employer and does not discriminate in employment opportunities or practices based on race (including traits historically associated with race, such as hair texture, hair type and protective hair styles (e.g., braids, twists, locs and twists)), color, religion, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions and lactation), sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age (40 and over), marital status, disability, genetic information, and protected veteran status or any other characteristic protected by applicable federal, state, or local law. For more information review the Two Six Technologies&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twosixtech.com/wp-content/uploads/Two-Six-EEO-Policy-Statement-2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://twosixtech.com/wp-content/uploads/Two-Six-EEO-Policy-Statement-2026.pdf&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1779469372739000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw0K5XXzO_7gnJKivjcSTuLG&quot;&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Policy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #262626; font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twosixtech.com/wp-content/uploads/TST-EEO-Know-Your-Rights-2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://twosixtech.com/wp-content/uploads/TST-EEO-Know-Your-Rights-2026.pdf&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1779469372739000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1NhroTC2YrHmuZp-gsYbBI&quot;&gt;EEO Poster&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you are an individual with a disability and would like to request reasonable workplace&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;il&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/span&gt; for any part of our employment process, please send an email to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations@twosixtech.com&quot;&gt;accommodations@twosixtech.com&lt;/a&gt;. Information provided will be kept confidential and used only to the extent required to provide needed reasonable accommodations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Additionally, please be advised that this business uses E-Verify in its hiring practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting the following application, I hereby certify that to the best of my knowledge, the information provided is true and accurate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Two Six Technologies, we build, deploy, and implement innovative products that solve the world’s most complex challenges today. Through unrivaled collaboration and unwavering trust, we push the boundaries of what’s possible to empower our team and support our customers in building a safer global future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Director, Cybersecurity Engineer,&lt;/strong&gt; you will provide hands-on technical leadership for a team researching and evaluating hardware and software solutions in support of defensive cyber operations. Drawing from military or government cyber mission experience, you will lead the assessment of engineering prototypes, validate their operational utility, and translate customer needs into practical technical plans. Solutions may include specialized network sensors, hardware networking devices such as FPGA-based firewalls, and software written in languages such as Rust or Python. You will direct technical teams while remaining engaged in technical analysis, testing, and customer collaboration. Vulnerability research may be part of the work when customer requirements call for it. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an onsite role based in the Two Six Technologies Laurel, Maryland office, with approximately 20% travel, including customer meetings in Arlington and Herndon as-needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mentor technical leads, each managing one to two staff or senior personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As the team grows, participate in hiring, performance management, and career development for team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical priorities and plans for research, evaluation, and validation of hardware and software solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply defensive cyber operations experience to assess mission needs, operational constraints, and candidate solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and oversee testing of engineering prototypes, including test procedures, measures of effectiveness, and analysis of results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct hands-on technical analysis and testing when needed, and guide teams through complex technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical findings, risks, and recommendations to customers, leadership, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with customers and internal stakeholders to shape requirements and align work to mission needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support vulnerability research when customer requirements call for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable technical processes and documentation for evaluations and test activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant professional experience in one or more related areas, such as incident response, vulnerability research, network engineering, or software development OR comparable experience and education will be considered.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage technical staff or leads, set priorities, and mentor senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting military or government defensive cyber missions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience researching, evaluating, or validating cybersecurity hardware or software solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and conducting technical testing of systems, devices, or engineering prototypes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to present findings and recommendations to technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret clearance with SCI eligibility or access (TS/SCI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cyber operations platforms, defensive tools, network technologies, or security monitoring systems such as Zeek, Snort/Suricata, Splunk, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating specialized network sensors, hardware networking devices such as FPGA-based firewalls, or software written in Rust or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting engineering research and development or prototype transition into operational use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with vulnerability assessment or research methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading the delivery of successful contracts to military or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Clearance Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret clearance with SCI eligibility or access (TS/SCI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MS1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two Six Technologies is committed to providing competitive and comprehensive compensation packages that reflect the value we place on our employees and their contributions. We believe in rewarding skills, experience, and performance. Our offerings include but are not limited to, medical, dental, and vision insurance, life and disability insurance, retirement benefits, paid leave, tuition assistance and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
