&lt;p&gt;Two Six Technologies is seeking a Language Enabled Analyst (Spanish) to support a US Government customer. This position will involve leveraging language and cultural understanding to develop effective messaging strategies across a variety of social media platforms, engaging with individuals in those global locations, studying data from various social media platforms and other online sources, assessing content validity, and writing reports detailing these assessments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job Responsibilities Include:&lt;br&gt;• Develop and implement messaging strategies for propagating messaging content in target language information environment(s) via various social media presences; engage with individuals in target language on behalf of the program&lt;br&gt;• Collaborate with a variety of stakeholders to align messaging strategies with program priorities&lt;br&gt;• Write long-form analytical reports that summarize findings to be disseminated to multiple stakeholders&lt;br&gt;• Assess content in target language or dialect for potential intelligence value&lt;br&gt;• Analyze a wide variety of OSINT information&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;br&gt;• Native proficiency in Spanish; fluency in French and/or Arabic strongly preferred&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated expertise in Foreign Terrorist Organizations (FTOs), Transnational Criminal Organizations (TCOs), and drug trafficking organizations (DTOs), including their organizational structures, operational activities, networks, and evolving threats.&lt;br&gt;• Minimum of 3 years writing grammatically and culturally appropriate content in target language without peer review&lt;br&gt;• Minimum of 3 years in an intensive academic or professional background in target region political and/or security issues&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with traditional and social media in target language, including prevalent trends, key personalities, political dynamics, and current events&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated use of target language in either an IC mission set or in an IO/OSINT mission set.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated advanced professional writing skills in the English language&lt;br&gt;• Experience and demonstrated proficiency using a range of technologies, including databases and open-source tools&lt;br&gt;• Local to NOVA or willing to relocate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice If You Have:&lt;br&gt;• Background in data science and programming languages&lt;br&gt;• HUMINT/Targeting experience or experience in cybersecurity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clearance Requirements:&lt;br&gt;• Active TS/SCI clearance&lt;/p&gt;
