&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Two Six Technologies, we build, deploy, and implement innovative products that solve the world’s most complex challenges today. Through unrivaled collaboration and unwavering trust, we push the boundaries of what’s possible to empower our team and support our customers in building a safer global future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two Six Technologies is actively seeking a Lead Embedded Software Engineer to join our team in Arlington, Virginia. The team is composed of intelligent, driven individuals, passionate about vulnerability analysis and RF-enabled exploitation who are rapidly developing novel capabilities that enable real-world missions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is growing and looking for someone with a practical software development background who has an understanding of how to transition cyber proofs-of-concept into operational, fieldable capabilities to support national security missions.&amp;nbsp; Strong candidates will also possess experience with RF protocols and/or software-defined radio development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide thought leadership -- plan, design, and direct the execution of high-level software tasks for rapidly developing bespoke fieldable capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the software team – direct multidisciplinary engineering teams through task management and technical oversight, delivering software for advanced RF platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly transition research-grade, “proof-of-concept” software, and vulnerability analysis findings from the lab to real-world use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop flexible, well-tested software modules which can be rapidly assembled into mission-customized solutions for immediate fielding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide expert guidance to human and agentic team members across a variety of technical domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;When needed, support real-world missions on-site in real time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will need (basic qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer/Electrical Engineering, or a related Scientific Domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5 years of hands-on experience in Python as well as C/C++ or Rust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software architecture experience -- demonstrated track record of success in taking ideas “from whiteboard to fielded”, observing best practices and thorough testing throughout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux, containerization, networking, administration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess excellent organizational, communication, and time management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to adapt and learn new skills to meet the needs of the mission and your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret Clearance with the ability and willingness to obtain and maintain a TS/SCI, and ability to work on-site in Arlington, VA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have (preferred)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RF and/or DSP (radio frequency and digital signal processing).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with radio protocol reverse engineering, data science/intelligence analysis, distributed systems, cryptography, GPU programming, UI/UX development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with low-level hardware reverse engineering (can read schematics, tap communications buses, leverage JTAG for introspection on unfamiliar systems, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of leveraging agentic engineering to deliver stable, well-designed, maintainable and well-documented solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s or Graduate degree in Computer Science, Computer/Electrical Engineering, or a related Scientific Domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Clearance:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active Top Secret Clearance willing to obtain and maintain a TS/SCI clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
