&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Two Six Technologies, we build, deploy, and implement innovative products that solve the world’s most complex challenges today. Through unrivaled collaboration and unwavering trust, we push the boundaries of what’s possible to empower our team and support our customers in building a safer global future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced Senior Platform Software Engineer (AI Specialist)&amp;nbsp; to join our core Platform Team. Our platform functions as a curated, self-service product designed to accelerate delivery and reduce cognitive load for our Stream-Aligned feature teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be the primary architect and technical owner of our internal AI orchestration ecosystem. You will not build isolated features; instead, you will design, deploy, and maintain the underlying infrastructure, developer tools, and shared services that enable full-stack feature developers to seamlessly integrate agentic AI capability into their codebases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, hybrid position that requires work at our Arlington office three days per week. Applicants must be U.S. citizens and have the ability to obtain and maintain up to a Top Secret/SCI security clearance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own AI Infrastructure &amp;amp; Orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish, scale, and maintain a robust internal orchestrator layer to manage LLM interactions, tool execution loops, context windows, and token allocation efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Self-Service Tools &amp;amp; Libraries:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and package shared utilities, client libraries, and standardized abstractions (such as managed agentic skills and database migration patterns) so feature teams can independently leverage AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize for Fast Flow:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Stream-Aligned developers to evaluate, select, and optimize prompt engineering guardrails, embedding stores, and testing patterns, ensuring automated pipelines protect flow and speed up deployment frequency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Platform Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure platform components are hosted independently, version-controlled, and seamlessly importable, allowing for safe rollbacks and clean operational boundaries within a monorepo structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate and Upskill:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in internal guilds and cross-team workshops, acting as a technical consultant to ensure architectural decisions across the UI, API, and data model layers remain fluid and stable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
